AQE: its a framework for which is used for reoptimising the query execution plan during runtime.it was introduced in spark 3.0
main features:

applying coalesce to the partition to combine smaller partition into a single partition to save space 

(example: several smaller partition while applying wide transformation may result smaller partition along with large partition.
with help of coalesce it combines smaller partition into bigger partition to decrease number of partition and improve query execution space/time)

minimise skewness by breaking up bigger partition into small chunks during execution

(example: large partition offers skewness.with AQE the large partition is divided into several small similar partition to eliminate skewness)

applying required filters before joining to minimise data size and apply boradcast join

(example: sparks normal joins are expensive if used which are mostly merger sort join. 
AQE helps in minimising the size of the data set to a small chunk to apply broadcast join with the large dataset)
